# Domain class comments

Class docs are ontology, not an API guide.

- One block above the class: English name + Russian term, then a few lines on
  what it is, who owns it, and lasting invariants.
- Do not narrate the lifecycle step-by-step when method names already do.
- Comment a method only when the contract is non-obvious from the name and
  signature; never restate the signature in prose.
- Prefer cutting comments over growing them when the type is thin.
